{
  "comment": "How one conversation is run (D-304): when Claude Code is started, with which arguments, what is written to it and what goes into the log. Claude Code is played from the script: each entry waits for one thing (start, user, response, interrupt, mode), writes its lines and may end the process. The setup is the same for every scenario: the environment Work, the conversation id-1, the folder /work. A start is described by whether it resumes and by the mode it carries. The log lines are what ITerminalLog was told, never a text of the conversation.",
